{% doc %}
  Outputs one word for a campaign metaobject (SHO-169): `active`, `upcoming`,
  `ended`, `restricted` for an email-link-only campaign (Liquid can't tell
  who arrived through the link, so the theme never advertises one), or
  `invalid` when it can't be shown honestly (no dates, dates the
  wrong way round, no badge, offer or terms). Capture it to branch on it.

  The same rules as packages/shopify/src/campaign.ts, which web and the app
  use: live from starts_at up to, not including, ends_at. Metaobjects don't
  switch themselves off, so this is where the dates are enforced.

  The "Campaign preview time" theme setting stands in for now, to check a
  campaign before it starts. Leave it empty on the live theme.

  @param {object} campaign - A `campaign` metaobject.

  @example
  {% capture status %}{% render 'campaign-status', campaign: campaign %}{% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  if settings.campaign_preview_at != blank
    assign now_s = settings.campaign_preview_at | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  endif
  assign start_s = campaign.starts_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign end_s = campaign.ends_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0

  if campaign == blank or start_s == 0 or end_s <= start_s
    echo 'invalid'
  elsif campaign.badge.value == blank or campaign.offer.value == blank or campaign.terms.value == blank
    echo 'invalid'
  elsif campaign.audience.value == 'email_link'
    echo 'restricted'
  elsif now_s < start_s
    echo 'upcoming'
  elsif now_s < end_s
    echo 'active'
  else
    echo 'ended'
  endif
-%}
